From: Micromium <micromium@example.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Android PAC/BTI hardening (Micromium)

- Enables pointer-authentication (PAC) + branch-target-identification (BTI)
  guards on arm64 via -mbranch-protection where the NDK clang supports it
- Enforces CFI on the Android build by default
- Enforcement GN flags live in android/args.gn; this patch flips the
  upstream defaults so a plain `gn gen` stays hardened.

Rebased against Chromium 153.0.8010.27 (branch 1681091).

--- a/build/config/android/config.gni
+++ b/build/config/android/config.gni
@@ -9,5 +9,10 @@
 declare_args() {
+  # Micromium (Android): PAC/BTI + enforced CFI on arm64 (see android/args.gn).
+  micromium_android_cfi_enforced = true
+  micromium_android_branch_protection = true
   # Build incremental targets whenever possible.
   # See //build/android/incremental_install/README.md for more details.
   incremental_install = false
+  # Micromium (Android): hardened-build marker, surfaced in chrome://version.
+  micromium_android_hardened_marker = true
 }
